              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "Analyse the examples to identify the rule:\n- In each row, 0s located between two non-zero pixels (of the given color) are filled with color 2 (red).\n- Wait, let's verify each example:\n  - Example 1:\n    Row 1: [1] to [7] are 3 -> between them, cols 2,3,4,5,6 become 2.\n    Row 2: [2] and [6] are 3 -> cols 3,4,5 become 2.\n    Row 3: [3] and [5] are 3 -> col 4 becomes 2.\n    Row 4: single 3 -> no 2s.\n  - Example 2:\n    Row 0: cols 5 and 7 are 4 -> col 6 becomes 2.\n    Rows 1-4: only one 4 -> no 2s.\n    Row 5: cols 0 and 7 are 4 -> cols 1,2,3,4,5,6 become 2.\n  - Example 3:\n    Row 0: cols 1, 4, 8 are 8 -> between 1 and 4 (cols 2,3) become 2; between 4 and 8 (cols 5,6,7) become 2.\n    Row 1: cols 2, 5, 7 are 8 -> cols 3,4 become 2; col 6 becomes 2.\n    Row 2: cols 3, 6 are 8 -> cols 4,5 become 2.\n    Row 3: cols 4, 5 are 8 -> adjacent, no 0s between.\n  - Example 4:\n    Row 2: cols 2 and 4 are 1 -> col 3 becomes 2.\n    Row 3: cols 1 and 5 are 1 -> cols 2,3,4 become 2.\n    Row 4: cols 0, 3, 6 are 1 -> cols 1,2 become 2; cols 4,5 become 2.\n    Row 6: cols 1, 2, 5 are 1 -> cols 3,4 become 2 (between 2 and 5).\n\nSo the rule is:\nFor each row, fill the 0s that lie between the first and last non-zero pixel of that row with 2.\nWait, is it between ANY pair of non-zero pixels, or just between first and last?\nIn all examples:\nBetween every pair of consecutive non-zero pixels in the same row, if there are 0s between them, they become 2.\nSince it covers all 0s between the first non-zero pixel and the last non-zero pixel of that row, it's simply:\nFor each row with at least two non-zero pixels:\nLet c_min be the index of the first non-zero pixel, and c_max be the index of the last non-zero pixel.\nEvery 0 between c_min and c_max is replaced by 2.\n\nI am ready for the test input. Please provide it.",
